# Lieutenant Commander  

  

## Overview  

  

Lieutenant Commander is a senior officer rank within Eagle Fleet. Officers holding this rank are typically experienced department heads aboard starships and starbases, executive officers of smaller vessels, or senior staff officers within fleet commands.  

  

Lieutenant Commanders are expected to lead personnel effectively, manage complex operations, and prepare for higher command responsibilities.  

  

## Rank Information  

  

| Category | Value |  

|----------|--------|  

| Rank | Lieutenant Commander |  

| Abbreviation | LCDR |  

| Grade | Senior Officer |  

| Superior Rank | [[07 Commander]] |  

| Junior Rank | [[09 Lieutenant]] |  

| Typical Posting | Department Head, Executive Officer, Senior Staff Officer |  

  

## Responsibilities  

  

- Leading major departments aboard ships and stations  

- Supervising officers and enlisted personnel  

- Managing operational and administrative functions  

- Advising senior command staff  

- Coordinating mission planning and execution  

- Training and mentoring junior officers  

  

## Authority  

  

A Lieutenant Commander exercises authority over assigned personnel and resources and may assume command when required by operational necessity or established command protocols.  

  

## Typical Assignments  

  

- Chief Operations Officer  

- Chief Engineering Officer  

- Chief Medical Officer  

- Chief Science Officer  

- Executive Officer, Small Vessel  

- Senior Staff Officer  

  

